      "title": "Understanding Letter-Numbers",
      "explanation": "Letter-numbers are symbols like 'a' or 'n' used to represent numbers in expressions. Algebraic expressions containing these letter-numbers, such as 'a + 3', are called algebraic expressions. They allow us to express mathematical relations concisely.",
